^"threads"{
  valence = `prime-11 through -17, -20: Boon HONK, boon bane bone, Boon PI; the September 27 valence folios (03, 13, 16, 19, 20, 22, 23) are its earlier pages.`
  rooms = `prime-00 (spwashi.com, lore.land, factshift.com), the Lore.Land sign in prime-05 through -09, and Production for Lore.Land: each arc has up to 13 beats.`
  operator_table = `prime-01 through -05 carry the Lore.land operator table: ~ Potential, # Vibration, . Ground, ? Wonder, ! Action, * Value, & Subject, @ Perspective, <> Concept, () Scene, [] Mode, {} Structure, ^ Integration, numbered 0–12 and lettered A–M. It is recorded as lettered. Where it meets the site's one character table (kernel/operator-detection.js; .spw/language/operator-namespace-alignment.spw) is the creator's call: history, dialect, or canon.`
  lens = `Pick a lens, highlights relevant topics and features (prime-14 through -19), with a lens picker of sigils; the site's lens instrument and the lenses-as-Spw-scripts plan answer the same sketch.`
  wap = `prime-18 (LIKE I AM WAPBOY) and prime-20 (when a clown receives a pie to the face, WAP) join Wonder About Pi(e).`
  practice = `1. Practice 2. Operationalize 3. Boon HONK (prime-11 through -15); September 27 folio 17 practice-collaborating-communication.`
  calendar = `prime-21, April 01 through 30 with a heart and a hash mark each; scrap-01 dated 5/17/22; September 27 front 09 (October 09, Monday).`
  journey = `prime-05, -08, -10: first an Electrical Engineer, now planning with Claude, GPT, Grok, and Gemini; HTML in 2011 to architecture by 2015; fifteen/sixteen years of dev motion.`
}

^"imagine"{
  creator = `2026-09-28: later, some of these go to Grok Imagine; prime the assets to be explorable in a more compelling way.`
  seat = `Each sidecar carries ^"imagine": status, a motion drawn from the piece, the neighbours it shares cutouts with (after, before, shares), where returns land, and an empty derivatives list.`
  seed = `Send the master as scanned. Imagine reads a dark ground more predictably than transparency; the clear tier is for the page.`
  returns = `public/images/renders/imagine/2026-09-28/<slug>-imagine-NN.<ext>. The renders/ path marks them generated (~) by rule, and each sidecar names generator: Grok Imagine and source: the piece id, so every generated picture points back at its scan.`
  keeps = `Generated motion garbles lettering. The scan stays the reading layer: a page shows Imagine's motion and settles back on the scan, never the reverse, and alt text always describes the scan.`
  sequence = `The primes in scan order are already a stop-motion of rearrangement. The most compelling first experience is a scrubber across prime-01 to -20: cutouts that stay hold still, cutouts that arrive fade in, a reader can pin one * handle and follow it, and an Imagine clip plays in the gap between two neighbours that share cutouts. The rail's motion between Spw positions is the same problem at page scale.`
  feel = `The scrubber, its timing, and which clips return are a feel decision: a flagged demo, approved in a browser before anything ships.`
}

^"held"{
  words = `Some lettering is personal or frank: prime-04 (my ex got hotter), prime-06 and -09 (what makes new friends feel scared, old friends feel helpless), prime-13 through -16 (crush, soul mate, post-nut clarity; the avoidant attachment playbook). Alt text transcribes it; whether a piece is shown, and where, is the creator's call.`
  schooling = `prime-07 letters: I attended the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign and majored in Learning and Education Studies. The alt text transcribes the piece; no page copy restates it.`
  placement = `unset on routes. A flagged demo, /design/experiments/folios/primes/, steps the twenty-five primes with no script (radio frames the arrow keys move through, a cutout to follow, a ground to choose), linked only from the folio experiments hub, /design/experiments/folios/. The folio shelf or a single weekly piece stay open.`
}
